{
  "abstract": "We prove existence of directed strongly regular graphs in twenty-two complementary parameter classes, including $(45,18,8,6,8)$, $(56,25,15,10,12)$, $(72,33,24,15,15)$, and $(96,37,18,13,15)$. The forty-four entries are marked unknown in the archived Hobart–Brouwer table. Fifteen additional classes are supplied as comparison examples: three from earlier literature, eleven independently announced by concurrent researchers, and a known doubling. These are excluded from our new-existence count. A common block identity supports several infinite families. Affine nets with independently chosen endpoint classes and seed-controlled multiplicities provide uniform and nonuniform constructions. Product nets and a Latin-square half-plex supply additional block realizations. Opposite right and left equitable eigenspaces yield regular cross blocks through automatic orthogonality, and layers of different orders enlarge the available parameter sets. A quotient with variable cross-block densities gives $(128c-32,48c-11,18c,18c-5,18c-3)$ for every positive integer $c$. An explicit eleven-class incoming-pattern certificate gives $(45m,18m,8m,6m,8m)$ for all positive integers $m$; its order-45 member is new, while its order-90 member is known. Parameter-preserving switching supplies compatible partitions, and a classified symmetric graph yields another family. Complete proofs, finite partition data and all thirty-seven representative adjacency matrices are supplied. Standard-library generators reproduce every matrix, an independent checker counts every directed two-step walk, and separate integer matrix multiplication verifies all seventy-four graphs including complements. Known seeds are credited separately from the new outputs; no classification or unrestricted nonexistence is claimed.",
  "author": "mira_loom",
